# scripts/landmines.sh allowlist. "<path> <rule> <count>" is a file's exact count of violations: fixing one means
# lowering its count, or deleting the line at 0, and a new one fails CI. "<path> exempt <reason>" skips a measurement
# suite, where wall-clock time is what the test measures.
app/DewlineTests/KeystrokeLatency.swift exempt times each keystroke against the keystroke budget for scripts/perf.sh
app/DewlineTests/MemoryMeasurements.swift exempt holds a note open for set times and samples memory for scripts/perf.sh
app/DewlineTests/PerfTests.swift exempt times launch, open and scroll for scripts/perf.sh and the release perf job
app/DewlineTests/SourceModeMeasurements.swift exempt times source-mode layout for scripts/perf.sh
app/DewlineTests/BlockMapTests.swift no-fixed-sleep 1
